{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-11-06T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A volcano, a rainforest and a bamboo grove? Haleakalā National Park on Maui has all three. Spanning Maui from its 3,055-metre summit to the coast, the park protects landscapes that change dramatically with elevation, rainfall and temperature. It was established in 1916 as part of Hawaii National Park and became its own national park in 1961. The name Haleakalā translates to 'House of the Sun', reflecting the Hawaiian mo'olelo of Māui capturing the Sun to lengthen the day.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PipiwaiTrail_EN-IN0566152296_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PipiwaiTrail_EN-IN0566152296_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A green tunnel through Maui","Title":"Bamboo forest, Pīpīwai Trail, Haleakalā National Park, Maui, Hawaii, USA","Copyright":"© MNStudio/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/20.760987,-156.155095/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=20.760987,-156.155095;S9;Haleakalā National Park, Maui, Hawaii&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261106_PipiwaiTrail\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Haleakala+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261105_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261106_PipiwaiTrail"},"Ssd":"20261106","Name":"PipiwaiTrail","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"0566152296","FullDateString":"6 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A simple wooden stile leads into one of England's most celebrated landscapes. The Lake District, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, is a patchwork of shimmering lakes, rugged fells and centuries-old stone walls, all shaped by both nature and farming traditions.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.StileCrossing_EN-IN0635462552_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.StileCrossing_EN-IN0635462552_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"One step closer to the summit","Title":"Wooden stile at a stone wall, Black Crag, Lake District, England","Copyright":"© Alex Treadway/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/54.460861,-3.08875/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=54.460861,-3.08875;S9;Lake District, England&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261105_StileCrossing\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lake+District&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261104_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261105_StileCrossing"},"Ssd":"20261105","Name":"StileCrossing","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"0635462552","FullDateString":"5 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"People paddle through a glowing maze of bald cypress in Xuancheng, Anhui, where autumn transforms flooded woodlands into a tapestry of amber, copper and deep rust. Known scientifically as 'Taxodium distichum', bald cypress is unusual among conifers because it sheds its soft, feathery needles each fall, turning reddish-brown before they drop.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AutumnChina_EN-IN9898936239_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AutumnChina_EN-IN9898936239_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Paddling a painted forest","Title":"People rowing among colourful bald cypress, Xuancheng, Anhui, China","Copyright":"© Jackal Pan/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/30.9525,118.75528/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=30.9525,118.75528;S9;Xuancheng, Anhui, China&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261104_AutumnChina\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=bald+cypress&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261103_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261104_AutumnChina"},"Ssd":"20261104","Name":"AutumnChina","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9898936239","FullDateString":"4 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Lake Braies sits almost 1,500 metres above sea level in the Dolomites of South Tyrol, northern Italy. Surrounded by forest and the dramatic peaks of the Fanes-Sennes-Braies Nature Park, the lake is known for its striking green and blue waters. A 3.5-kilometre trail circles the shore, while traditional wooden rowing boats offer another way to take in the scenery. The lake is also a starting point for several mountain walks, including the Dolomites' famous Alta Via 1.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AlpineBraies_EN-IN9491975263_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AlpineBraies_EN-IN9491975263_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Peace among the peaks","Title":"Lake Braies, Fanes‑Sennes‑Braies Nature Park, Dolomites, Italy","Copyright":"© leonid_tit/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/46.693566,12.084606/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=46.693566,12.084606;S9;Lake Braies, Fanes‑Sennes‑Braies Nature Park&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261103_AlpineBraies\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lake+Braies+Dolomites&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261102_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261103_AlpineBraies"},"Ssd":"20261103","Name":"AlpineBraies","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9491975263","FullDateString":"3 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"These polar bears are gathering along the shores of Hudson Bay in Manitoba, Canada, waiting for sea ice to form so they can head back out to hunt seals. That annual spectacle inspired Polar Bear Week, observed during the first week of November, a celebration of the Arctic's largest land predator. Polar bears are powerful swimmers, expert hunters and remarkably adapted to life in one of Earth's harshest environments. Yet shrinking sea ice means many spend longer on land, making it harder to find food and raising the risk of encounters with people.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.HudsonBear_EN-IN9299365522_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.HudsonBear_EN-IN9299365522_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A future written in ice","Title":"Polar bear and cubs by Hudson Bay, Manitoba, Canada","Copyright":"© Danita Delimont/Adobe Stock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"In a single season, a polar bear may cover more than 1,000 kilometres while searching for food and suitable ice.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261102_HudsonBear\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Polar+Bear+Week&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261101_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261102_HudsonBear"},"Ssd":"20261102","Name":"HudsonBear","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9299365522","FullDateString":"2 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today we're enjoying the misty views sweeping across the Black Forest, which stretches for around 160 kilometres across south-west Germany, bringing together wooded hills, deep valleys, lakes and charming towns. Its highest point, Feldberg, rises to 1,493 metres, while the Black Forest is also the starting point for the Danube and Neckar rivers. There's plenty of history and tradition here too. Forestry has long played an important role in the region, while its centuries-old clockmaking heritage helped make the distinctive cuckoo clock famous far beyond Germany.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SchwarzwaldAutumn_EN-IN9123894203_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SchwarzwaldAutumn_EN-IN9123894203_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Mist among the trees","Title":"Black Forest, Baden-Württemberg, Germany","Copyright":"© Britus/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/48.286722,8.215281/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=48.286722,8.215281;S9;Black Forest, Baden-Württemberg&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261101_SchwarzwaldAutumn\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Black+Forest+Germany&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261031_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261101_SchwarzwaldAutumn"},"Ssd":"20261101","Name":"SchwarzwaldAutumn","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9123894203","FullDateString":"1 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Forget the fog machine. Frankfurt, Germany, has something far more effective: a Gothic cathedral with a tower that looks ready for a midnight séance. St Bartholomew's Cathedral, seen here, has the medieval silhouette Halloween practically ordered for itself. But the festival's own history is even stranger.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FrankfurtHalloween_EN-IN8941917618_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FrankfurtHalloween_EN-IN8941917618_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Ghosts of empires past","Title":"St Bartholomew's Cathedral in Frankfurt, Germany","Copyright":"© AlxeyPnferov/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/50.110766,8.68539/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=50.110766,8.68539;S9;St Bartholomew's Cathedral, Frankfurt&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261031_FrankfurtHalloween\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Halloween&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261030_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261031_FrankfurtHalloween"},"Ssd":"20261031","Name":"FrankfurtHalloween","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8941917618","FullDateString":"31 Oct, 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As the Sun dips towards the horizon, the Damodar River becomes a gathering place for Chhath Puja. The four-day Hindu festival is dedicated to Surya, the Sun God, and Chhathi Maiya. Mainly observed in Bihar, Jharkhand and Uttar Pradesh, as well as parts of Nepal, it is a celebration of gratitude for the Sun and its life-sustaining energy. Devotees observe fasting and gather beside rivers and other bodies of water to pray. One of the festival's most distinctive traditions is offering prayers to both the setting and rising sun, creating striking scenes as families and communities gather at the water's edge at dusk and dawn.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ChhathPuja2026_EN-IN6558699033_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ChhathPuja2026_EN-IN6558699033_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":false},"Headline":"Glow of Chhath Puja","Title":"Sunset over the Damodar River during Chhath Puja","Copyright":"© ParthapratimMukherjee2056/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/23.480162,87.290903/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=23.480162,87.290903;S9;Damodar River&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261113_ChhathPuja2026\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Chhath+Puja&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261112_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261113_ChhathPuja2026"},"Ssd":"20261113","Name":"ChhathPuja2026","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"6558699033","FullDateString":"13 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Just north of Moab, Utah, Arches National Park is home to more than 2,000 natural sandstone arches – the densest concentration of arches in the world. Today's image, North Window, is one of the best-known formations in the park's Windows Section, where towering fins, openings and sculpted sandstone create a landscape that looks almost architectural.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.NorthWindow_EN-IN3919602543_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.NorthWindow_EN-IN3919602543_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Architecture without an architect","Title":"North Window, Arches National Park, Moab, Utah, USA","Copyright":"© lightphoto/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/38.6857117,-109.5328291/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=38.6857117,-109.5328291;S9;North Window, Arches National Park, Moab, Utah&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261112_NorthWindow\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Arches+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261111_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261112_NorthWindow"},"Ssd":"20261112","Name":"NorthWindow","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"3919602543","FullDateString":"12 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The Atlantic Forest is one of the world's great biodiversity hotspots, stretching along much of Brazil's Atlantic coast and into Argentina and Paraguay. Its landscape includes tropical and subtropical forests, mangroves and coastal habitats, providing a home for around 20,000 plant species and an extraordinary variety of wildlife, including jaguars and golden lion tamarins. Much of the forest has disappeared over the centuries, but it continues to play an important role in storing carbon and providing fresh water for millions of people across the region.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Atlantica_EN-IN3149189379_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Atlantica_EN-IN3149189379_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A forest full of wonder","Title":"The Atlantic Forest, Brazil","Copyright":"© FG Trade/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"The Atlantic Forest is home to around 150 million people, which is roughly a third of South America's total population.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261111_Atlantica\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Atlantic+Forest+Brazil&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261110_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261111_Atlantica"},"Ssd":"20261111","Name":"Atlantica","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"3149189379","FullDateString":"11 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"From above, Rose Island looks like a brushstroke of green surrounded by every shade of blue. Just five kilometres east of Paradise Island in The Bahamas, this slender cay trades busy roads and city blocks for sandy shores, shallow waters and an inland lagoon. Its peaceful appearance comes with a touch of movie drama. Rose Island was used as a filming location for the 1965 James Bond adventure 'Thunderball', including the explosive destruction of the Disco Volante.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.RoseIsland_EN-IN1259562642_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.RoseIsland_EN-IN1259562642_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Licensed to chill","Title":"Aerial view of Rose Island, The Bahamas","Copyright":"© Abstract Aerial Art/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/25.088243,-77.225304/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=25.088243,-77.225304;S9;Rose Island, The Bahamas&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261110_RoseIsland\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Rose+Island+Bahamas&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261109_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261110_RoseIsland"},"Ssd":"20261110","Name":"RoseIsland","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"1259562642","FullDateString":"10 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Cross the Guadalquivir River in Seville, the capital of Spain's Andalusia region, and the city's rhythm seems to change. On the other side lies Triana, a colourful neighbourhood where ceramics, flamenco and local traditions are woven into everyday life. Since the 19th century, the Isabel II Bridge, also known as the Triana Bridge, has connected the neighbourhood to Seville's historic centre.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.TrianaSpain_EN-IN5231956941_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.TrianaSpain_EN-IN5231956941_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where art finds its rhythm","Title":"Historic district of Triana, Seville, Spain","Copyright":"© Andrzej Rostek/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/37.382904,-6.006341/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=37.382904,-6.006341;S9;Triana, Seville, Spain&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261109_TrianaSpain\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Seville+Spain&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261108_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261109_TrianaSpain"},"Ssd":"20261109","Name":"TrianaSpain","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"5231956941","FullDateString":"9 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Across India, Diwali brings homes, streets and neighbourhoods to life with the warm glow of lanterns, diyas and colourful decorations. Known as the Festival of Lights, it celebrates themes of hope, new beginnings and the triumph of light over darkness. Traditions vary across the country, but for many families, the festivities include creating rangoli, performing Lakshmi Puja, exchanging sweets and gifts, and spending time with loved ones. Diwali is also associated with Lord Rama's return to Ayodhya after defeating Ravana. More than a festival, it's a time for togetherness, reflection and welcoming the year ahead with optimism.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.DiwaliLamps_EN-IN0900276687_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.DiwaliLamps_EN-IN0900276687_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Happy Diwali!","Title":"Lanterns for Diwali in Mumbai, Maharashtra","Copyright":"© Dinodia Photo/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/18.969048,72.821182/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=18.969048,72.821182;S9;Mumbai, Maharashtra&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261108_DiwaliLamps\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Diwali&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261107_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261108_DiwaliLamps"},"Ssd":"20261108","Name":"DiwaliLamps","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"0900276687","FullDateString":"8 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Bison are among the largest land mammals in the world, capable of weighing up to 900 kilograms and reaching speeds of 65 kilometres per hour despite their massive size. Despite often being called a buffalo, the American bison is not one of the true buffaloes, which are native to Africa and Asia. Its scientific name, Bison bison, leaves little room for confusion.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.DakotaBison_EN-IN0635434875_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.DakotaBison_EN-IN0635434875_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Roaming the grasslands","Title":"A bison in the grasslands of Theodore Roosevelt National Park, North Dakota, USA","Copyright":"© Tandem Stock/Adobe Stock","SocialGood":null,